        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trudge/{size}/2062_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-27T23:51:15.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Do you think we'll eventually see every hero belonging to a canonical team?&nbsp; With Freedom Four/Five/Six, the Dark Watch, and the Prime Wardens, somewhere over half the existing heroes are on a team.&nbsp; And the Sentinels <em>are</em> a teams.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The teams that already exist seem to hit tropes from existing team comics.&nbsp; The Freedom Five hit a lot of JLA tropes (and also some Fantastic Four tropes, with Tachyon and Freedom Tower reminding me of Reed Richards and the Baxter Building).&nbsp; The Dark Watch evokes a lot of the Spiderman Team Up comics, in which he frequently worked with heroes like Daredevil, Punisher, and Doctor Strange.&nbsp; The Prime Wardens reminds me of an early Defenders line up (Dr. Strange, Hulk, Namor, Silver Surfer, Valkrie -&gt; Agent Adept, Haka, Tempest, Captain Cosmic, Fanatic)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Sentinels Tactics Uprising sort of makes an (unnamed) team out of Visionary, Beacon, and Unity, and because of their age they seem kind of like the Teen Titans or Young Avengers.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:24.813Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
